      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a90cde143233e50c3cf5235",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "I think this new motion should be the secondary option.  Even if it works reliably on some controllers, it still gives people like me motion sickness.  Might be fine for most but for sensitive types it's a loss of control that starts messing with your head.  \n\nBut what puzzles me is how this is working for others.  Obviously it can't be what I'm experiencing with my (vive) setup or I don't think the devs would have green lit this.  I've tried for hours today, and am still dizzy from the efforts, to find a consistent method of moving short distances, or even long ones, but it feels almost random.  Sometimes it keeps moving forward indefinitely, other times it stops after a bit.  And if I tap it quickly, it sometimes moves a bit, othertimes indefinitely.  \n\nI know they're working on bringing back the old system for some, as it's the best navigation in vr imho, but I'm genuinely curious for whom it is working better as I'm sure it must be.  Is it aimed more at Oculus?  Or do some vive owners have zero issues, and it's some sort of lag thing that throws it off?  My internet is genuinely very fast, but vrchat for some reason, lately, has slowed down with this ISP.  So maybe that's part of the problem?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
